00:29:38.376 --> 00:29:41.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
The trial of Kermit Gosnell
which I talk about in my book,

00:29:41.179 --> 00:29:43.515
probably the greatest serial
killer in American history,

00:29:43.515 --> 00:29:45.683
an abortion doctor who delivered

00:29:45.683 --> 00:29:47.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
thousands upon
thousands of babies.

00:29:47.919 --> 00:29:51.389
He sniffed the spinal cords
of babies about to be born,

00:29:51.389 --> 00:29:53.258
late term abortionist.

00:29:53.258 --> 00:29:55.260
And his trial was suppressed.

00:29:55.260 --> 00:29:57.896 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was hardly any
news coverage of it.

00:29:57.896 --> 00:30:00.331
America's greatest
serial killer, why?

00:30:00.331 --> 00:30:02.233 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because if the network
went wall to wall

00:30:02.233 --> 00:30:05.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
with coverage of that trial,
it actually made people

00:30:05.236 --> 00:30:07.839
think twice about being
pro-life or pro-choice.

00:30:07.839 --> 00:30:10.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in a newsroom, that's
yucky to have people

00:30:10.642 --> 00:30:12.777 align:start size:81% position:19%
who think pro-life
be legitimized.

00:30:12.777 --> 00:30:15.280 align:start size:88% position:13%
Nobody thinks like
that inside a newsroom.

00:30:15.280 --> 00:30:18.016
So there was an absence
of coverage and again,

00:30:18.016 --> 00:30:20.752
this is what gave
way to Fox News.

00:30:20.752 --> 00:30:22.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
Fox said, you're only
telling one side of a story,

00:30:22.887 --> 00:30:24.422
you're leaving on the
cutting room floor

00:30:24.422 --> 00:30:25.924
so much of American life.

00:30:27.425 --> 00:30:29.828
