00:39:20.124 --> 00:39:22.993
you must be like, man, I
wish my guy would've got

00:39:22.993 --> 00:39:25.796 align:start size:88% position:13%
the long leash that
they're giving this guy.

00:39:25.796 --> 00:39:28.032
- Yeah, George Bush used to
joke that he had some issues

00:39:28.032 --> 00:39:29.333
with the English language.

00:39:30.501 --> 00:39:32.636
I think they call it
the American language

00:39:34.038 --> 00:39:38.576 align:start position:0%
but it was always convivial
and he had inarticulate moments

00:39:40.144 --> 00:39:41.846 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I don't think
anybody questions his
leadership strength

00:39:41.846 --> 00:39:45.449 align:start size:97% position:3%
or his decision making or
the toughness of his policies

00:39:45.449 --> 00:39:48.252
or his integrity and
that was a difference.

00:39:49.487 --> 00:39:50.988
- Are you still in touch with,

00:39:50.988 --> 00:39:52.656
I assume you're still in
touch with President Bush.

00:39:52.656 --> 00:39:55.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
And are you surprised that
he went so apolitical?

00:39:55.292 --> 00:39:57.895 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I know most presidents
do but he really has just,

00:39:57.895 --> 00:39:59.397
he enjoys painting it seems like

00:39:59.397 --> 00:40:00.931
and living on the ranch

00:40:00.931 --> 00:40:02.767
and just doesn't have much to
do with public policy anymore.

00:40:02.767 --> 00:40:04.201
- You know, one of
the things about him,

00:40:04.201 --> 00:40:07.171
he always understood
that he was gonna go in

00:40:07.171 --> 00:40:08.739
and get out himself.

00:40:08.739 --> 00:40:10.741
Now I remember during
the recount in 2000

00:40:10.741 --> 00:40:12.276
when Al Gore was
working the phones

00:40:12.276 --> 00:40:15.012
and trying to influence votes
in Florida during the recount,

00:40:15.012 --> 00:40:17.681 align:start size:84% position:16%
George Bush was at
his ranch cutting wood

00:40:17.681 --> 00:40:19.817
and people thought
he was disengaged.

00:40:19.817 --> 00:40:21.218
He wasn't disengaged,

00:40:21.218 --> 00:40:23.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
he always had this
healthy sense of removal.

00:40:23.921 --> 00:40:25.790
He would go back to
the mansion at night

00:40:25.790 --> 00:40:28.759
with his briefing book for
the next day and watch ESPN.

00:40:29.960 --> 00:40:32.129
You know, I do think he
just had a healthy sense

00:40:32.129 --> 00:40:34.999
of who he was, criticism
would roll off his back.

00:40:34.999 --> 00:40:37.468
He was a strong leader
who made big decisions

00:40:38.903 --> 00:40:43.507
but he didn't sweat the typical
Washington insider nonsense.

00:40:43.507 --> 00:40:45.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that kept
him a lot better in touch

00:40:45.609 --> 00:40:46.877
with the country.

00:40:46.877 --> 00:40:48.512
- I'd like to finish
up with something else

00:40:48.512 --> 00:40:50.414
because I've wanted to have
you on for quite some time

00:40:50.414 --> 00:40:52.082
and we were trying to
get you on last year

00:40:52.082 --> 00:40:56.287
for the 9/11 anniversary
and you usually on 9/11,

00:40:56.287 --> 00:40:59.390
you do a full Twitter recap
of what that day was like

00:40:59.390 --> 00:41:01.225 align:start size:97% position:3%
and being with the President
and everything else.

00:41:01.225 --> 00:41:03.060
I lived in New York
City at the time,

00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:05.996
much of my family lived in
New York City at the time.

00:41:05.996 --> 00:41:08.399 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I remember you, I
remember obviously George Bush

00:41:08.399 --> 00:41:10.434 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I remember Rudy Giuliani
and all of those things,

00:41:10.434 --> 00:41:12.069
all of those people.

00:41:12.069 --> 00:41:13.904
Can you just talk a
little bit about that

00:41:13.904 --> 00:41:17.141
and maybe I can get you
back on in a couple weeks

00:41:17.141 --> 00:41:20.277
in September to do a
bigger dive on that

00:41:20.277 --> 00:41:21.745 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I just think it's
important to talk about.

00:41:21.745 --> 00:41:24.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, you know Dave,
when I look back the thing

00:41:24.014 --> 00:41:25.816 align:start size:97% position:3%
that strikes me having been
at the President's side

00:41:25.816 --> 00:41:28.452 align:start size:97% position:3%
for much of that day and
being on board Air Force One

00:41:29.620 --> 00:41:33.624 align:start size:84% position:16%
was how unemotional
it was for those of us

00:41:33.624 --> 00:41:37.461
with the president which is I
think in many ways remarkable

00:41:37.461 --> 00:41:39.196
'cause it was probably
the most emotional day

00:41:39.196 --> 00:41:40.898
anybody alive today has had.

00:41:42.800 --> 00:41:44.235
And it had to be that way.

00:41:44.235 --> 00:41:47.404 align:start position:0%
You know, everybody, the
President was kinda just steely

00:41:47.404 --> 00:41:50.841
like this, the secret service
around him, steely like that,

00:41:50.841 --> 00:41:54.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
the military like that,
it was such a seriousness,

00:41:54.311 --> 00:41:55.946
a steadiness.

00:41:55.946 --> 00:41:58.282
And I was at the
President's side

00:41:58.282 --> 00:42:00.985 align:start size:88% position:13%
when he said to the vice
president, we at war.

00:42:00.985 --> 00:42:03.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he called the
secretary of defense

00:42:03.053 --> 00:42:06.390
and said to the secretary
of defense, were at war

00:42:06.390 --> 00:42:09.426
and it just sent a
chill down my spine.

00:42:09.426 --> 00:42:12.229 align:start size:84% position:16%
And looking back,
some people might say,

00:42:12.229 --> 00:42:14.932
well, of course, we're
at war, we were attacked.

00:42:14.932 --> 00:42:16.500
Well, the next day
in the cabinet room,

00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:17.468
when the president
held the meeting

00:42:17.468 --> 00:42:18.702
with congressional leaders,

00:42:18.702 --> 00:42:21.572 align:start size:88% position:13%
all of whom were
tremendously supportive.

00:42:21.572 --> 00:42:24.508
One leader said to the
President, the Democrat,

00:42:24.508 --> 00:42:26.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
I urge you to use
caution in your rhetoric,

00:42:26.577 --> 00:42:28.178
war is such a scary word.

00:42:29.380 --> 00:42:30.814
And I just remember
thinking to myself,

00:42:30.814 --> 00:42:33.584
if this isn't war, what is?

00:42:33.584 --> 00:42:35.586 align:start size:88% position:13%
The decision of the
President to tell people

00:42:35.586 --> 00:42:40.591
that we're at war sent
the direction to everyone

00:42:41.992 --> 00:42:44.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
to start planning for
what we were going to do.

00:42:44.194 --> 00:42:47.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was the right
and necessary step to take

00:42:47.898 --> 00:42:51.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it reoriented everything
we've done since then.

00:42:51.402 --> 00:42:54.038 align:start size:97% position:3%
It put us on a much stronger
ground against terrorism,

00:42:54.038 --> 00:42:55.573
it's one of the reasons
we haven't been hit again

00:42:55.573 --> 00:42:57.107
in a major attack.

00:42:57.107 --> 00:43:00.511
It influenced our thinking
about growing strikes abroad

00:43:00.511 --> 00:43:03.147
which have been carried out
now not only by George Bush

00:43:03.147 --> 00:43:06.884 align:start size:97% position:3%
but by Barack Obama,
Donald Trump and Joe Biden.

00:43:06.884 --> 00:43:09.153
It created a bipartisan template

00:43:09.153 --> 00:43:11.021
for how to protect this country,

00:43:11.021 --> 00:43:13.023
all of which came from
the strength I think

00:43:13.023 --> 00:43:16.961
that he exhibited that day
but it was a time of the,

00:43:20.664 --> 00:43:24.101 align:start size:97% position:3%
just the utmost seriousness,
the utmost weight

00:43:24.101 --> 00:43:25.603
on our shoulders.

00:43:25.603 --> 00:43:28.539
We were told by the CIA,
it's not a question of if,

00:43:28.539 --> 00:43:31.909
it's a question of when
the second wave will be

00:43:33.110 --> 00:43:34.812
and that permeated
all our thinking.

00:43:34.812 --> 00:43:39.516 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Let's finish up
flash forwarding now
21 years into 2022.

